node_modules/
dist/
# .coherence/ holds two DIFFERENT kinds of thing, and they need opposite treatment.
# verify-jobs.json is regenerated on every run and is genuinely a cache. decisions/
# and status.json are the RECORD — the decision journal and the sticky red history,
# both cumulative, both worthless if a fresh clone starts empty. A blanket ignore was
# defensible when this directory held only transient files; it stopped being defensible
# the moment the journal landed here, and this repo was ignoring the very folder its
# own README tells consumers to commit.
.coherence/*
!.coherence/decisions/
!.coherence/status.json
!.coherence/calibration/

# AGENTS.md and public/{graph.json,_graph.html,_overview.html} are committed, fully-owned
# reading surfaces now that this repository has a real spec tree. `coherence docs --check`
# gates their freshness; the other public artifacts are independently generated and already
# tracked where their commands own them.
